1
00:00:07,799 --> 00:00:14,047
Forty-one thousand people went to a football match in
Lyon on a Thursday evening in October,

2
00:00:14,067 --> 00:00:17,929
and at eight fifty-two the doors
closed from the outside.

3
00:00:18,329 --> 00:00:24,086
The narrator will not dwell on who they were or what
they wanted, because the world has

4
00:00:24,106 --> 00:00:29,863
heard enough about them and because the only thing
that matters to this account is what

5
00:00:29,883 --> 00:00:35,906
they had: seven people, automatic weapons, four
vehicle-borne devices at the vehicle gates,

6
00:00:35,926 --> 00:00:41,550
and control of a bowl containing forty-one thousand
human beings, nineteen hundred of

7
00:00:41,570 --> 00:00:42,479
them children.

8
00:00:42,880 --> 00:00:48,735
They made one demand at nine fifteen and they did not
repeat it. The French government's

9
00:00:48,756 --> 00:00:54,611
crisis unit assessed it as unsatisfiable by design,
which is the polite phrase for *they

10
00:00:54,631 --> 00:00:57,549
came here to kill everyone in
the building.*

11
00:00:57,950 --> 00:01:03,339
By half past ten the assault plan existed, and
the assault plan was appalling.

12
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:09,840
Four entrances, seven hostiles, four devices, no
reliable interior picture, and a crowd

13
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:15,891
that would panic the instant the first door came in.
The planning cell's own estimate,

14
00:01:15,911 --> 00:01:21,941
presented to the Minister at ten forty, was between
two and nine thousand dead if they

15
00:01:21,961 --> 00:01:25,530
went in, and everybody in the room
if they did not.

16
00:01:25,930 --> 00:01:31,966
At twenty-six fifteen, a man from the Direction
Générale de la Sécurité Intérieure who

17
00:01:31,986 --> 00:01:38,022
had spent three years quietly reading a file that
did not exist made a suggestion that

18
00:01:38,042 --> 00:01:44,078
got him removed from the room and then, forty
minutes later, got him brought back into

19
00:01:44,098 --> 00:01:44,289
it.

20
00:01:44,810 --> 00:01:46,120
Say it again.

21
00:01:46,519 --> 00:01:51,636
(flat) Umbrella has a response capability. Sixty-one
aircraft. Teams on eighteen-minute

22
00:01:51,656 --> 00:01:56,950
readiness. They contained Ravenna in sixty-one days
when we could not do it in six months.

23
00:01:57,349 --> 00:02:00,879
Ravenna was a *virus*. This is a stadium.

24
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:05,712
(flat) Minister, I am aware of what it is. I am
telling you that I have read four years

25
00:02:05,732 --> 00:02:10,063
of anomalies about that company, and that if there
is anything in the world which can

26
00:02:10,083 --> 00:02:14,414
walk through seven armed men without the crowd
knowing it has happened, it belongs to

27
00:02:14,434 --> 00:02:14,670
them.

28
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:20,553
The call was placed at three minutes past midnight.
It was answered on the second ring

29
00:02:20,573 --> 00:02:23,801
by a man who had been awake and
dressed for two hours.

30
00:02:24,322 --> 00:02:30,964
Minister. Before you ask, the answer is yes, and it
will take twenty-three minutes from

31
00:02:30,984 --> 00:02:35,711
the moment you say the words, and you
will not like the words.

32
00:02:36,111 --> 00:02:37,401
What words?

33
00:02:37,801 --> 00:02:44,322
That the Republic of France requests and authorises
the deployment of an Umbrella asset

34
00:02:44,342 --> 00:02:50,937
inside the Stade Belloy, and that the asset's methods
are at my discretion, and that you

35
00:02:50,957 --> 00:02:54,771
will say so on camera afterwards,
whatever happens.

36
00:02:55,171 --> 00:02:57,541
I cannot authorise a private —

37
00:02:57,942 --> 00:03:04,815
Minister, there are nineteen hundred children in that
building and your own planning cell

38
00:03:04,835 --> 00:03:11,553
has told you that going in costs you two thousand
people. I am not negotiating and I am

39
00:03:11,573 --> 00:03:18,292
not going to help you find a form of words that lets
you deny this tomorrow. Say it, or

40
00:03:18,312 --> 00:03:18,912
hang up.

41
00:03:19,861 --> 00:03:26,466
The recording of that call was released in 2041 and
has been studied ever since. The pause

42
00:03:26,486 --> 00:03:28,012
is nine seconds long.

43
00:03:28,532 --> 00:03:31,901
(very slow) The Republic of France
requests the deployment.

44
00:03:32,301 --> 00:03:33,111
Thank you.

45
00:03:33,512 --> 00:03:38,721
He turned to Hale, and what he said next is the
sentence that changed the century.

46
00:03:39,241 --> 00:03:41,131
Wake T-103.

47
00:03:41,972 --> 00:03:47,205
The narrator asks you to understand what was in that
cradle, because for eight years it

48
00:03:47,225 --> 00:03:49,741
had been an air conditioner in a basement.

49
00:03:50,141 --> 00:03:55,818
Two point nine metres. Three hundred and forty
kilograms. Grey, bald, expressionless,

50
00:03:55,838 --> 00:04:01,983
with hands that could take a car door off its hinges, a
nervous system that had been rebuilt

51
00:04:02,003 --> 00:04:07,947
to ignore pain and a conditioning that made obedience
simpler than breathing. It had been

52
00:04:07,967 --> 00:04:11,431
designed, in another world, to be
dropped on a city.

53
00:04:11,831 --> 00:04:18,501
It had never been used. In eight years it had left
its cradle four times, always in an

54
00:04:18,521 --> 00:04:24,802
empty hall at Arklay, always for twenty-three
minutes, always under Wesker's eye.

55
00:04:25,201 --> 00:04:31,238
At eighteen minutes past midnight on the nineteenth
of October 2035, it walked up a ramp

56
00:04:31,258 --> 00:04:37,295
into an Umbrella transport aircraft in western
Pennsylvania wearing a grey overcoat that

57
00:04:37,315 --> 00:04:42,182
had been made for it by a tailor who had
been told it was for a statue.

58
00:04:42,581 --> 00:04:49,004
Flight time to Lyon: four hours forty. It sat in the
hold, upright, in a restraint frame,

59
00:04:49,024 --> 00:04:50,597
and did not move once.

60
00:04:50,997 --> 00:04:56,706
At twenty-three minutes past five in the morning, the
east tunnel doors of the Stade Belloy

61
00:04:56,726 --> 00:04:58,216
opened from the outside.

62
00:04:58,617 --> 00:05:04,105
There were nine hundred police officers, four
television crews with long lenses at two

63
00:05:04,125 --> 00:05:09,934
hundred metres, and a French colonel who had been told
what was coming and had not believed

64
00:05:09,954 --> 00:05:10,127
it.

65
00:05:10,526 --> 00:05:15,576
What walked in was three metres tall, wore a
grey overcoat, and did not hurry.

66
00:05:15,976 --> 00:05:19,427
Four minutes. The narrator will
account for all of them.

67
00:05:19,826 --> 00:05:25,221
In the first minute it crossed the tunnel and
entered the north concourse, where three

68
00:05:25,241 --> 00:05:30,824
of the six were positioned. They fired. The footage —
and there is footage, from a police

69
00:05:30,844 --> 00:05:36,616
camera on a pole outside, of the muzzle flashes through
the tunnel mouth — shows the flashes

70
00:05:36,636 --> 00:05:39,387
stop, one by one, over about
eleven seconds.

71
00:05:39,786 --> 00:05:44,927
In the second minute it went up the internal stair
to the executive level and took the

72
00:05:44,947 --> 00:05:50,326
two who were holding the stadium's control room, and
turned off the public address system,

73
00:05:50,346 --> 00:05:54,226
which had been playing the same recorded
message for eight hours.

74
00:05:54,627 --> 00:06:00,029
In the third minute it went along the second tier,
where three of them had spread out

75
00:06:00,049 --> 00:06:05,578
above the crowd, and this is the part that the world
argued about for a decade: not one

76
00:06:05,598 --> 00:06:11,256
shot was fired into the stands. Not one. Forty-one
thousand people sat in the dark, under

77
00:06:11,276 --> 00:06:16,805
a stadium roof, and heard, over the sound of their
own weeping, a series of very brief,

78
00:06:16,825 --> 00:06:20,697
very definite noises above them that
they could not identify.

79
00:06:21,096 --> 00:06:26,737
In the fourth minute it went to the vehicle gates and
dealt with the two who were sitting

80
00:06:26,757 --> 00:06:32,270
with the devices, and it did that part in such a way
that the devices did not function,

81
00:06:32,290 --> 00:06:37,803
and the narrator does not know how, and neither did
the French, and neither did anybody

82
00:06:37,823 --> 00:06:42,636
at Umbrella except one man in Singapore
watching on a handheld camera relay.

83
00:06:43,476 --> 00:06:47,637
At five fifteen and forty seconds, the
stadium lights came on.

84
00:06:48,036 --> 00:06:52,057
And forty-one thousand people saw what was
standing in the centre circle.

85
00:06:52,456 --> 00:06:58,023
It did not speak. It had no capacity to speak. It
stood in the middle of the pitch with

86
00:06:58,043 --> 00:07:03,931
its arms at its sides and its face turned up towards
the north stand, and it waited, because

87
00:07:03,951 --> 00:07:08,427
it had been given an instruction and the
instruction was not finished.

88
00:07:08,826 --> 00:07:10,257
The instruction had been:

89
00:07:10,776 --> 00:07:17,501
Clear the building. Then stand in the centre of the
pitch, in the open, where they can

90
00:07:17,521 --> 00:07:22,207
all see you, and do not move until the
last person has left.

91
00:07:22,607 --> 00:07:28,493
The east and west gates opened. Nine hundred police
came in and did not know what to do.

92
00:07:28,513 --> 00:07:34,400
And forty-one thousand people filed down the stairs
and out past a monster that had just

93
00:07:34,420 --> 00:07:40,575
saved their lives and that watched them go, and did not
move, for two hours and twenty-three

94
00:07:40,595 --> 00:07:41,112
minutes.

95
00:07:41,511 --> 00:07:46,649
The last to leave were the children from the school
group in the north stand, because

96
00:07:46,669 --> 00:07:51,929
their teachers had made them wait until the stairs
were clear. There is a photograph of

97
00:07:51,949 --> 00:07:57,634
it — the most reproduced photograph of the twenty-first
century — taken by a nineteen-year-old

98
00:07:57,654 --> 00:07:59,941
with a telephone from the second tier.

99
00:08:00,341 --> 00:08:06,630
A line of eighteen-year-olds, walking out in pairs.
And in the background, out of focus,

100
00:08:06,650 --> 00:08:12,940
on the grass, in a grey overcoat: three metres of
engineered soldier, standing perfectly

101
00:08:12,960 --> 00:08:14,661
still, watching them go.

102
00:08:15,610 --> 00:08:22,293
Casualties: the eighteen. Hostages killed: none.
Hostages injured: forty-one, all in the

103
00:08:22,313 --> 00:08:25,721
initial crush at nine o'clock,
all recovered.

104
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:31,310
The world had nine hours to decide what it
thought, and it decided in about two.

105
00:08:31,831 --> 00:08:35,900
(broadcast) — we're going to show the photograph
again, and I'd ask you to look at the

106
00:08:35,920 --> 00:08:39,942
children rather than at the — at the figure.
Because that's the whole argument, isn't

107
00:08:39,962 --> 00:08:43,081
it. That's the entire argument of the next
ten years in one frame.

108
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:48,132
(broadcast) The French interior minister confirmed at
eight this morning that the Republic

109
00:08:48,152 --> 00:08:52,595
requested the deployment. He was asked seventeen
times what the asset was and gave the

110
00:08:52,615 --> 00:08:55,190
same answer each time: an Umbrella
security asset.

111
00:08:55,591 --> 00:08:57,240
(broadcast) And Umbrella?

112
00:08:57,640 --> 00:09:01,894
(broadcast) Six lines. I'll read the whole
statement. *At the request of the Government

113
00:09:01,914 --> 00:09:06,217
of France, an Umbrella security asset entered the
Stade Belloy at 5:11 this morning. All

114
00:09:06,237 --> 00:09:10,589
hostages are alive. The asset has returned to
Umbrella custody. We will not be discussing

115
00:09:10,609 --> 00:09:14,961
its nature, now or in future. Umbrella's medical
teams remain in Lyon for as long as they

116
00:09:14,981 --> 00:09:15,550
are needed.*

117
00:09:15,951 --> 00:09:17,401
(broadcast) That's it?

118
00:09:17,801 --> 00:09:22,040
(broadcast) That's it. No conference. No
photographs. The chief executive hasn't been

119
00:09:22,060 --> 00:09:22,291
seen.

120
00:09:22,691 --> 00:09:28,920
The narrator notes that the silence was worth more than
any speech Adolf could have designed,

121
00:09:28,940 --> 00:09:34,901
that Wesker knew it, and that when the passenger in
his skull suggested a stadium address

122
00:09:34,921 --> 00:09:38,261
in Lyon within the week, the
answer was two words.

123
00:09:38,780 --> 00:09:40,331
Absolutely not.

124
00:09:40,730 --> 00:09:44,298
They would carry you through the streets.

125
00:09:44,700 --> 00:09:51,299
Yes. And in four days a philosophy professor in
Berlin would write a column asking what

126
00:09:51,319 --> 00:09:58,071
else is in the basement, and he would be right, and
the carrying would stop. A crowd that

127
00:09:58,091 --> 00:10:03,929
has just been frightened must be allowed to
finish being grateful in private.

128
00:10:04,330 --> 00:10:10,471
Umbrella's stock fell sixteen per cent on the Monday
and recovered all of it by Thursday.

129
00:10:10,491 --> 00:10:16,633
The United Nations Security Council held an emergency
session on the Tuesday and produced

130
00:10:16,653 --> 00:10:19,610
nothing. Nineteen governments
opened files.

131
00:10:20,009 --> 00:10:25,745
And four hundred million people looked at a
photograph of a line of children and a grey

132
00:10:25,765 --> 00:10:31,435
giant, and understood, without anyone having to say
it, that the world had changed and

133
00:10:31,455 --> 00:10:35,139
that it had changed in a direction
nobody had voted for.

134
00:10:35,539 --> 00:10:41,092
The narrator will give you the part of Lyon that the
Directorate never quoted, because

135
00:10:41,112 --> 00:10:46,665
it appeared in a local newspaper in November and was
reprinted four thousand times and

136
00:10:46,685 --> 00:10:51,589
is the reason the word *Tyrant* never once
appeared in an Umbrella document.

137
00:10:51,990 --> 00:10:57,921
A primary school four streets from the Stade Belloy
asked its pupils, as schools do, to

138
00:10:57,941 --> 00:11:04,010
draw something about the week. Eleven of the nineteen
children in one class drew the same

139
00:11:04,030 --> 00:11:09,825
thing: a tall grey man in a coat, standing still,
with small figures walking past him

140
00:11:09,845 --> 00:11:10,509
in a line.

141
00:11:10,909 --> 00:11:16,720
One of them, aged eight, wrote underneath it, in the
careful handwriting of somebody who

142
00:11:16,740 --> 00:11:22,351
has just learned to join letters: *le monsieur qui
attend* — the gentleman who waits.

143
00:11:22,751 --> 00:11:28,884
It was on the front page of a regional paper on the
ninth of November. By the fourteenth

144
00:11:28,904 --> 00:11:33,847
it had been reproduced in nine countries. By
Christmas there were toys.

145
00:11:34,576 --> 00:11:41,455
Umbrella issued no statement, licensed nothing, and
sued nobody, which Catherine Adeyemi

146
00:11:41,475 --> 00:11:44,277
argued about for four days and lost.

147
00:11:44,797 --> 00:11:49,730
There are nine manufacturers in three countries making
an unlicensed plush toy of a biological

148
00:11:49,750 --> 00:11:54,210
weapon, and our legal position is unanswerable, and
you are telling me to do nothing.

149
00:11:54,610 --> 00:11:56,860
I am telling you to do nothing.

150
00:11:57,259 --> 00:11:57,975
Why?

151
00:11:58,375 --> 00:12:04,543
(very cold) Because a company that sues a child's
drawing has told the world what the

152
00:12:04,563 --> 00:12:10,875
drawing is. In four years every seven-year-old in
Europe will own a grey man who stands

153
00:12:10,895 --> 00:12:17,063
in front of them and waits, and in twenty years
those children will be voters, and in

154
00:12:17,083 --> 00:12:23,832
forty they will be ministers, and not one of them will
ever be able to be properly frightened

155
00:12:23,852 --> 00:12:24,705
of us again.

156
00:12:25,426 --> 00:12:34,380
I could not buy that, Ms. Adeyemi. It cost me five
dead men and four minutes and it was

157
00:12:34,400 --> 00:12:34,896
free.

158
00:12:35,296 --> 00:12:42,272
The narrator notes that he was correct, that the toy
is still manufactured, and that the

159
00:12:42,292 --> 00:12:49,189
Assembly's 2141 debate on the Veth included a speech
in which a delegate from Lyon held

160
00:12:49,209 --> 00:12:49,746
one up.

161
00:12:50,895 --> 00:12:59,585
Event. First deployment. Forty-one thousand hostages
recovered. Seven hostile casualties.

162
00:12:59,605 --> 00:13:08,587
Global awareness of Umbrella biological assets: total.
Fear, thirty-one per cent. Gratitude,

163
00:13:08,607 --> 00:13:17,296
fifty-eight. Both, seventy-four. Six million Points.
Level seventy-eight. Unlocked: Viral

164
00:13:17,316 --> 00:13:19,253
Dominion, level one.

165
00:13:19,722 --> 00:13:27,476
Viral Dominion permits direct command of any organism
carrying your viral lineage, without

166
00:13:27,496 --> 00:13:33,091
an intermediary, at a range of
approximately four hundred metres.

167
00:13:33,490 --> 00:13:38,020
I have never needed one. It does
what it is told.

168
00:13:38,421 --> 00:13:44,931
It does what Hale tells it, through a conditioning
that was designed by people who are

169
00:13:44,951 --> 00:13:52,069
dead in a world that no longer exists. You have never
once given that thing an order yourself.

170
00:13:52,909 --> 00:13:55,799
(very cold) No. I have not.

171
00:13:56,200 --> 00:14:01,678
He stood in the hangar at three in the morning,
alone, and looked up at it in its frame.

172
00:14:01,698 --> 00:14:06,490
Three metres. Pale eyes, open, watching him and
nothing else in the building.

173
00:14:06,889 --> 00:14:12,546
He had bought it out of a lottery for nine thousand
Points in 2027 and he had been afraid

174
00:14:12,566 --> 00:14:18,349
of it for about two seconds and had enjoyed that, and
in eight years he had never permitted

175
00:14:18,369 --> 00:14:23,898
himself to notice that he had left it in a basement
not because it was dangerous to the

176
00:14:23,918 --> 00:14:27,980
world, but because it did not, strictly
speaking, answer to him.

177
00:14:28,500 --> 00:14:29,690
Buy the Dominion.

178
00:14:30,720 --> 00:14:39,310
Purchase. Viral Dominion, level one. Four million.
Balance, nine million one hundred thousand.

179
00:14:39,899 --> 00:14:45,543
He looked up at the thing in the frame and, without
speaking, without moving, without

180
00:14:45,563 --> 00:14:51,340
any mechanism that he could describe afterwards to
Evelyn Marsh or to anyone else, told

181
00:14:51,360 --> 00:14:52,139
it to kneel.

182
00:14:53,090 --> 00:14:58,955
Three hundred and forty kilograms of engineered
soldier went down on one knee on a hangar

183
00:14:58,975 --> 00:15:04,643
floor at three in the morning, silently, in front of
a man in a black coat, and stayed

184
00:15:04,663 --> 00:15:05,040
there.

185
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:06,770
The other voice stirred.

186
00:15:07,289 --> 00:15:09,684
(very soft) There it is.

187
00:15:10,085 --> 00:15:10,655
Don't.

188
00:15:11,054 --> 00:15:17,621
I have waited nine years to see you do something
that was purely for yourself.

189
00:15:18,022 --> 00:15:23,883
The narrator notes that Albert Wesker stood in that
hangar for another twenty-three minutes,

190
00:15:23,903 --> 00:15:29,509
and that the Tyrant remained kneeling the entire
time, and that nobody else in the world

191
00:15:29,529 --> 00:15:34,432
